  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given plane $3 x+y+2 z+6=0$\r\nand line $\\frac{x-\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{2 b}{3}}=\\frac{y-3}{-1}=\\frac{z-1}{a}$\r\nSince, plane is parallel to line, then\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n& 3\\left(\\frac{2 b}{3}\\right)+(1)(-1)+2(a)=0 \\\\\r\n& 2 b-1+2 a=0 \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad a+b=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\r\n&\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nNow, $3 a+3 b=\\frac{3}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
